The train then drove right out of Berlin.
We left the last houses behind us.
Then we drove right into a dense forest.
We drove past many tall pines.
I looked out of the window for a long time.
Then I watched the other passengers in the carriage.
At one station, a few hikers got in.
They all wore sturdy shoes and backpacks.
They looked for free seats.
After that, a family with three children came too.
The children ran quite loudly through the aisle.
They shouted and laughed a lot.
The parents just walked slowly behind them.
The noise didn't bother me at all.
I just stayed relaxed in my seat.
We drove a bit further.
And then we arrived in Potsdam.
